    <td colspan=3 bgcolor="#D8F8F8" valign=top><font size=2>Wondering whether a mount will help you to avoid aggro/work with your playstyle? &nbsp;Try this part of a simple quest where you can try a horse once (norent). <br> &nbsp;<br> Copied from Alla's: <br> &nbsp;<br> Go to Befallen's first level and find a skeletal foreman. Kill him to spawn a ghost named Sir Ariam Arcanum. Hail him and he will tell you his story. &nbsp;<br> &nbsp;<br> You say, 'Hail, Sir Ariam Arcanum' &nbsp;<br> &nbsp;<br> Sir Ariam Arcanum says 'My thanks for destroying these minions of Befallen's masters' Sir Ariam's form suddenly contorts in agony. 'This accursed place rends my soul trying to twist me to its purposes. My time here is short.'' &nbsp;<br> &nbsp;<br> You say &quot;I sense a deep pain within you, ghost. Is there some way I might assist you so that you may find eternal rest?&quot; &nbsp;<br> &nbsp;<br> After that he will tell you more about his story and ask you to perform a task for him. &nbsp;<br> &nbsp;<br> You say &quot;I will perform any task that will cleanse this place.&quot; &nbsp;<br> &nbsp;<br> Sir Ariam Arcanum says 'I have this parchment that must be delivered to either the Knights of Truth in Freeport or to the Queen of Neriak. The contents of the note concern them both and I am desperate to have this matter addressed so ask that you take it to which ever of the cities will accept your presence. Will you take the note to the [Knights of Truth] or to [The Dead]?' &nbsp;<br> &nbsp;<br> Tell him which you will take it to and he gives you a note and ghostly birdle (No Drop/No Rent/Lore) that has one charge of Summon: Horse on it. He will tell you where to take it. &nbsp;<br> </font></td>
  </tr><tr>
